      "reason": "Rebuilding the Nino 3.4 index requires spatial averaging over a latitude-longitude box, and this fragment's guidance on weighted surface means constrains how the regional mean should be formed.",
      "status": "condensed",
      "notes": [
        "The region mean over 5S–5N, 170W–120W is a physical average: use `compute_basic_stat` with `op='area_weighted_mean'` (plain `op='mean'` weights every element equally), and restrict the weight to the same valid cells as the data so land/missing cells stay out of the denominator."
